[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/48992297","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/288#issuecomment-48992297","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/288","id":48992297,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4OTkyMjk3","user":{"login":"jswalden","id":4139753,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzk3NTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4139753?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden","html_url":"https://github.com/jswalden","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jswalden/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-07-15T05:34:22Z","updated_at":"2014-07-15T05:34:22Z","body":"`ExpressionChecker.infer_function_type_arguments` decides for `id(square)`, via `ExpressionChecker.get_arg_infer_passes`, that the function argument type should be resolved in the second pass.  Or something along those lines.  It then proceeds to use `None` as argument type, which \"type\" propagates via return value until the embedded argument type gets compared against `int` for the 1.\n\nIt's not immediately clear to me, looking at this code, why it shouldn't iteratively infer types until a fixed point is reached.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/48992297/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hoor